Please find the Q1 2021 inspection status for the ATU-100. Current activities are being tracked against the RBI intervals defined in QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 3, which specifies 3 years for Class 1 sour gas, regenerator overhead, and rich amine, and 6 years for the remaining lines.

The current baseline for the 150 CMLs across 18 lines is based on the UT thickness survey completed in LNDE-RPT-20191001-027-R0. We are monitoring these points to ensure compliance with the retirement thickness and remaining life calculations per site rules.

